  "nonmonotone_samples": 0,
  "statement": "rho depends on the direction only through u = n_xhat^2: R1, R2 are functions of (r, M, M') only; the Q_K numerator pieces carry (1-u) in term 1 and u in terms 2-4 and nothing else directional; alpha^2 carries u linearly and nothing else directional. Hence rho(u) at fixed r is a ratio of affine functions of u (monotonic), and rho*(r) = min over u in [0,1] is the exact angular minimum; rotation about the x-axis at fixed n_xhat leaves the evaluator input (r, u) unchanged."
